ct equality; `rho`, `rho_rel`, `rho_mono`, `iSupRho`, and `iSupRho_eq_id` are the injection–projection composites, the betweenness relation on neighbourhoods of \(\mathcal{D}\), monotonicity, and the union equal to the identity; `map_rho_heq` and `key_rho` give \(\rho_{n+1} = \mathrm{iso} \circ T(\rho_n) \circ \mathrm{iso}^{-1}\) with both legs of `colimIso` equal to identity morphisms; `nonempty_strict_algHom`, `nonempty_algHom`, and `exists_algebra_with_hom` produce a homomorphism into every algebra whose structure map is strict; `rho_zero_rel`, `strict_rel_master`, `gcomp_rho_zero_rel`, `gcomp_rho_zero_indep`, `gcomp_rho_succ`, `gcomp_rho_indep`, `gcomp_eq`, `algHom_unique`, and `exists_unique_strict_algHom` are the zero stage, the recursive step, and uniqueness of strict homomorphisms. The remaining stems `mem_cast`, `rec_trans`, `set_rec_trans`, `subsystem_cast`, `transport_heq`, `isoOfEq_conj`, `map_comp_proj_heq`, `algHom_ext`, `cat_comp_eq`, and `Basic` transport carriers and reassemble composition. `Setup.Γ` is an arbitrary neighbourhood system subject only to \(\Gamma \triangleleft T(\Gamma)\) after the carrier cast, and the first conjunct of `theorem_614` asserts an algebra with an isomorphism structure map together with a homomorphism into each strict-structure algebra; the unique-hom conjunct `exists_unique_strict_algHom` assumes in addition that every neighbourhood of the generator equals its master, which is the one-neighbourhood system \(\{\Gamma\}\) of the print and the hypothesis under which `rho_zero_rel` makes \(\rho_0\) send every neighbourhood to the master. `gcomp_eq` concludes that any two strict homomorphisms have the same underlying map because their composites with each \(\rho_n\) agree and \(\bigcup_n \rho_n\) is the identity, and `gcomp_rho_succ` writes \(h \circ \rho_{n+1} = k \circ T(h \circ \rho_n) \circ \mathrm{iso}^{-1}\); the print’s further claim that this \(h\) is the least fixed point of \(\lambda h.\, k \circ T(h)\) in \(|\mathcal{D} \to_\bot E|\) has no corresponding Lean statement. **Theorem:** partial — a fixed-point algebra and a strict homomorphism into every strict algebra exist for a general generator, while initiality is proved only after the generator is restricted to the one-neighbourhood system. **Proof:** partial — the tower, the union, both inclusions, the identity isomorphism, the betweenness description of \(\rho_n\), and \(\bigcup_n \rho_n = I_{\mathcal{D}}\) follow the print, while uniqueness is an induction on strict homomorphisms under the extra master hypothesis.
